  "notes": "University Park. Major code 'MATSCI' avoids colliding with the MATSE department prefix. Historical-year build (2026-09-17), fetched the real archived bulletin at the URL in 'source' above (raw HTML via curl, cross-checked against the page's own printed semester/fall/spring subtotals and 'minimum of 131 credits' program-requirements total, not WebFetch's summary) and compared it course-by-course against MATSCI-2026.json's already-verified structure. Program Requirements course list is byte-for-byte identical to 2024 and 2026 (structured diff of all 67 rows: no differences) -- same MATSE 436, same current Processing Laboratory numbering (MATSE 463/468/471/473), same 5-course elective lists in all three MATSE Specialization categories, same Entrance-to-Major requirements, same 12-credit Technical Elective pool, and the same 131-credit minimum. Carries over the 2026 plan's CHEM 110 -> MATH 22/21/4/3 remedial chain and 21-credit/semester cap unchanged, for the same reason given in the 2022/2023/2024 files' notes (chain re-verified directly against the 2022 archived MATH/CHEM course-description pages; wording identical to the current catalog and stable across editions). Real sequencing difference found and reflected structurally in this year's own bulletin (a genuine mid-history step, not present in 2022-2024 or yet fully matching 2026): this year's Suggested Academic Plan moves 'MATSE 413' out of Second Year Spring and into Third Year Spring -- the SAME semester the 2026 JSON already has it in (Semester 6) -- while 'IE 424 or STAT 401' is still in Second Year Spring here (this file's Semester 4), one edition before the live 2026 bulletin moves it to Fourth Year Fall. Since MATSE 413's real position this year already matches the existing 2026 JSON's Semester 6 placement, no change was needed there. For IE 424/STAT 401, kept this file's placement identical to 2026's (Semester 7) rather than moving it to Semester 4 to literally match this year's table, for the same reasons given in the earlier years' notes: it carries no tracked prerequisite in this app's IE/STAT catalog data, build_full_plan reports 0 scheduling warnings either way, and the 2026 file's Semester 7 placement (which also holds MATSE 436 and the Processing Laboratory item, both moved there for credit-cap-fitting reasons unrelated to this specific course) is already a deliberate rearrangement, not a literal per-year bulletin mirror.",
